{"creator_user_id": "927c6145-3816-445e-b96c-56f49cd1bef2", "id": "e53e61a6-e3e6-462b-b2ec-35727a3cb705", "isopen": false, "license_id": "notspecified", "license_title": "License not specified", "metadata_created": "2026-07-10T22:11:45.532089", "metadata_modified": "2026-07-10T22:11:45.532090", "name": "contracts-and-framework-agreements", "notes": "North Yorkshire County Council maintains a Contract Register, the purpose of which is to record key details of all Contracts with an aggregate value of £25,000 or more (excluding those related to individual packages of care). Whilst this register should be published on a quarterly basis, details are published in real time on Contracts Finder  https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Search and Yortender https://www.yortender.co.uk/

As recommended by the DCLG, this page also contains a copy of the Forward Procurement Plan (FPP) which is used by the Council to monitor procurement activity that will be required within the short term and long term to maintain services throughout North Yorkshire. 
